  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (A-PP-E-10-001 Rev C, A-PP-E-10-002 Rev B, A-PP-E-11-001 Rev B, A-PP-P-10-002 Rev C, A-PP-P-11-001 Rev C and Note in relation to parking provision and vehicular movemements  Received: 22 November 2017, A-PP-P-13-001 Rev D Received: 6th December 2017, Agent email dated 19th December 2017) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The mezzanine hereby approved shall be used for B2/B8 purposes ancillary to the use of the building within which it would be located and for no other purposes (including any other purpose in Class B of the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 or any other provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification).",
    "Condition : 4 - Full details of cycle parking to be submitted and approved prior to commencement of the hereby permitted development.  The cycle parking shall be implemented in accordance with the approved drawings prior to the occupation of the mezzanine hereby permitted and thereafter retained as such for the duration of the development.",
    "Condition : 5 - A) The development hereby permitted shall not commence until a sustainability statement has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local planning Authority.\r\nB) Prior to first occupation of the mezzanine hereby permitted an evidence pack shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority to show that the development has been constructed in accordance with the approved sustainability statement.\r\n"
  ],
